+List generators:
+================
+The list generators (`src/list/enumeration/`, include `list/enumeration/enumeration.h`)
+fill one or more lists with all `Element`s of a given shape: each `Value` of
+length `n` and weight `w`, and its `Label = HT * Value` (plus an optional
+syndrome in the first list). Consecutive values differ in one or two
+coordinates (Chase sequence for the support, Gray code for the nonzero
+symbols), so every label is computed with one or two additions instead of a
+full matrix vector multiplication. Optionally the labels of the first (and
+third) list are inserted into a hashmap, and a predicate can stop the
+enumeration early. All generators derive from `ListEnumeration_Meta`.
+- `ListEnumerateSingleFullLength`, `ListEnumerateMultiFullLength` (Fq),
+  `BinaryListEnumerateMultiFullLength`, `BinaryLexicographicEnumerator`
+  (binary): weight `w` (resp. at most `w`) on the full length `n`; with a
+  second list the same values are placed after the first `n` coordinates
+  (MITM).
+- `ListEnumerateSinglePartialSingle`, `ListEnumerateMultiDisjointBlock`,
+  `BinarySinglePartialSingleEnumerator`: four lists, a MITM part `[0, split)`
+  and a part `[split, n)` split into four blocks, so that the four lists
+  contain no representations of each other.
+
+Triple:
+=======
+`triple<T1, T2, T3, config>` (`src/container/triple.h`) is a packed 3-tuple
+(`first`, `second`, `third`), an extension of `std::pair`. The `ConfigTriple`
+allows to swap the field types and to set the alignment of each field, to
+experiment with the memory layout of list entries.
+

